name issue_24_timing_v2_render_fps
describe issue_53_cwnd_pushback with every v2 switch and libwebrtc's receive timing (timing v2): late frames are rendered, not dropped (issue #24)
duration 25s
at 0s  capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=100ms
at 8s  capacity=500kbps
cc v2
pacer v2
timing v2
# libwebrtc's VideoStreamBufferController skips a late frame only when a later
# temporal unit is already decodable (FrameDecodeTiming::OnFrameBufferUpdated,
# frame_decode_timing.cc:45); with every delta frame referencing the one before
# it, that is never the case, so late frames are decoded and shown. timing v1's
# FrameScheduler drops frames more than 10 ms late whenever a newer one is due.
# Seeds 1-10: timing v1 16.0-20.8 fps; timing v2 28.8-29.2; libwebrtc on
# issue_53_cwnd_pushback 27-28 (mean 27.5, parity-data main be4bfbc).
expect video.render_fps >= 28
expect video.residual_loss_pct <= 1.0
# Freezes: timing v1 2806-5621 ms, timing v2 1616-3793, libwebrtc 1512-4207.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 5000
